      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 896,
        "content": "## Autonomous Site Risk & Feasibility Analyst\n\n### How it works\n\nReceives site evaluation requests including location coordinates and radius via an n8n form.\nChecks whether coordinates fall on water and sends an immediate alert to Slack if the site is unbuildable.\nQueries external APIs to gather elevation profile, GBIF endangered species occurrences, and US Census socioeconomic metrics.\nAggregates all environmental and demographic metrics into a single unified JSON payload.\nAnalyzes the site with Google Gemini and an LLM Chain using structured output parsing.\nFormats and posts the resulting feasibility and risk report directly into Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Configure the Form Trigger node and share the submission URL.\n- - [ ] Add Google Gemini credentials to the Google Gemini Model sub-node.\n- - [ ] Connect Slack credentials and designate the recipient channels for water alerts and feasibility reports.\n- - [ ] (Optional) Provide a US Census API key if making high-frequency demographic queries.\n\n### Customization\n\nCustomize the Gemini prompt template and structured schema to evaluate domain-specific feasibility rules, or add further data sources like flood zones and solar irradiance."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
